    "letter": "I write as the registered keeper of vehicle MT24KPL in respect of Parking Charge Notice OR410109. I dispute liability for this parking charge and require the operator to consider this appeal.\n\nThe Parking Charge Notice alleges: Overstayed paid time at Oakridge Retail Quarter.\n\nOn the operator's own documents the parking event took place on 1 August 2026, the Notice to Keeper was issued on 25 August 2026; the statutory period for delivery of the notice ended on 15 August 2026 and it is deemed delivered on 27 August 2026, 12 days outside that period, so the notice was not delivered within the statutory period and keeper liability does not transfer.\n\nThe Notice to Keeper was not delivered within the applicable statutory period for the relevant postal-notice route. The operator has therefore failed to satisfy a condition required to transfer liability to the registered keeper under Schedule 4.\n\nThe operator has not established the identity of the driver. As the applicable Schedule 4 requirements have also not been satisfied, liability cannot be transferred to the registered keeper under Schedule 4.\n\nFor the reasons set out above, the parking charge is disputed and the operator is requested to cancel the Parking Charge Notice.\n\nThe operator has not established the identity of the driver. As the applicable Schedule 4 requirements have also not been satisfied, liability cannot be transferred to the registered keeper under Schedule 4. For the verified reasons set out above, the operator has not established keeper liability under Schedule 4 of the Protection of Freedoms Act 2012. The charge should therefore be cancelled as against the registered keeper. If the operator is not prepared to cancel the charge, it is requested to provide a clear response addressing the specific grounds and evidence raised.",
